value and  set the state and when we click on the  submit button the handle submit event  handler executes and we alert out the  current value printed in the text box  and that's it so how do you write  comments in react when you're a  developer if you want to comment out  some code or if you want to set comments  to enhance the maintainability of the  code a single line comment is as simple  as given in most other programming  languages backslash asterisk to open  astrix to close multi-line commands  follow the same syntax and can span  multiple slides to add comments to  functions in terms of what the function  can do and what are the types that it  can return what is the arrow function  and how is it used so an arrow function  is a shorter way of writing a function  in react if you look at the snippet on  the top my input on change equal to we  are connecting to this dot handle change  dot bind and that's the longer version  of how you can connect it to an event  handler the shorter version is on change  equal to e arrow operator this dot  handle on change so you don't need to  call the bind explicitly you can replace  that with the arrow operator and reduce  the amount of code that you typically  write how is react different from react  native so react and react native are  completely different react was released  in 2013 it's a web-based platform it is  html compliant it generates html views  it uses css for styling and it's based  on javascript html and css react native  on the other hand is targeted to  mobility devices it's meant to create  installable apps on android and ios  released in 2015 not based on html and  css and it basically requires the  react.js api to create these installable  apps for these mobility ecosystems how  is react different from angular another  popular framework by google so angular  created by google completely based on  the model view controller pattern works  on the real dom layer and requires a  full tree shake at the tom layer to  update views and components supports  bi-directional data mining the rendering  is purely done on the client side the  performance comparatively slow react.js  on the other hand created by facebook  it's the view layer of the model view  controller pattern it works at the  virtual dom layer and it sends faster  it's unidirectional data binding and not  two-way and the rendering is typically  what is done at the server side and what  you get is a response on the client as a  stream of html characters as an output  let's talk about and discuss some  questions around react components so  what are components in react so these  are the building blocks you can think of  them as lego blocks so you break your  problem down into small parts each part  identifying a certain solution of the  problem which is what we define as a  component so they are building blocks of  a react application and a single app  usually consists of multiple components  so it splits the ui into independent  reusable pieces that can be processed  separately a component is essentially a  piece of the user interface or the html  view what is the use of render method in  react so it is compulsory for each  component to have a render method if not  there wouldn't be any html for the  component to render on your view so the  render function returns the html which  is to be displayed within a component  like you see on the screen there is a  class app that extends the react  component and it returns a simple h1  element called hello simply learn and of  course do remember to export the app out  so that it can be accessed from other  components as well if you need to render  more than one element all the elements  must be inside a single parent tag like  a div or a form what is state in react  the state of a component is an object  that holds some data within it the data  would influence the output of the  component now how do you implement state  in react so state holds the data that a  component renders on the web application  for example here we've created in the  constructor this dot state equal to and  this temporary anonymous object has two  attributes car and pi when we return we  simply return this dot state dot car and  this dot state dot by now this is how  you would create stateful components and  access the state properties within the  view how do you update the state of a  component by using the built-in set  state method you can go ahead and update  the state of the component so here we  have a simple render function that  returns the state itself state dot  message and on the on click connects to  a button press function the moment you  click on the button the button press  function sets the state to another  message so the initial message in the  constructor is welcome to simply learn  the moment you click on the button the  set state triggers and changes it to  best place to learn so the data on the  view would be updated what are props in  react well props is just a short form  for properties and that is what allows  us to pass arguments or data to a  component props are passed to components  in the way similar to that of attributes  that are passed to an html element so  how do you pass props between two  components so let's say we have an  app.js component on the top and a  main.js component at the bottom at the  top we are trying to return this dot  props dot car and the bike so two car  and bike attributes associated with this  props of the app component in the main  component when you look at the render  function we are associating car prop  equal to a value of 1 600 cc and bike  prop equal to value of 150cc  and to access it if you look at the  import statement we are importing app  from  app.jsx and this is how you can  cross-access properties from one  component within the other so what are  the difference between state and props  well state holds information about the  components they are mutable they can be  changed they cannot be accessed by child  components and they cannot have state  props allow to pass data from one  component to the other as an argument  they are immutable they are read-only  and props can be accessed by the child  component and they can have props as  well what is a higher order component in  react so these act as a container for  other components which helps in keeping  components simple and induces the  reusability factor they are generally  used when a common logic has to be used  by multiple components that's when you  group together a set of components  within a higher order component in react  how can you embed two or more components  into one this code snippet demonstrates  the app component which returns a hello  text and it has a custom tag called  simple the simple tag is defined in the  component below and it returns text  called simply learn and in the render of  the react dom uh we simply go and render  the app component so hello simply learn  would be the final output and that's how  you can embed one component into the  other using this methodology what are  the differences between class and  functional components so stateful  components would extend react component  in this case and if you could look at  the render it simply renders  this.props.title  the constant stateless component would  be equal to props the div tag returns  this dot props dot title so you can look  at the style very different in terms of  class and functional components one  using the arrow operator one using the  traditional class and render method so  the class component can hold or manage  state complex as compared to stateless  components can work all of the life  cycle methods of the component and it  can be reused the functional component  cannot hold a managed state they are  simple and easy to understand it does  not work with any life cycle method and  it cannot be reused let's explain the  life cycle methods of components we've  got kenish initial state which is  executed before the creation of the  component component did mount which is  executed when the component gets  rendered and placed on the dom should  component update which is invoked when a  component decides any changes to the dom  and returns true or false value based on  certain conditions component did update  it is invoked immediately after the  rendering takes place component will  unmount which is invoked immediately  before a component is destroyed and  unmounted permanently let's move to the  react redux set of questions so what is  redux it's an open source javascript  library used to manage application state  and react uses redux for building the  user interface what are components of  redux the first is the store which holds  the state of the application  store contains state which defines the  user interface which triggers a set of  actions which are then sent to the  reducer so store holds the state action  is the source information for the store  and reducer specifies how the  application state changes in response to  actions sent to the store what is flux  well flux is the application  architecture that facebook uses for  building web applications and it works  in this way the action is triggered  which is sent to the dispatcher the  dispatcher sends it to the store the  store sends it to the view and the view  sends it back to the action and that's  exactly how the steps would continue in  sequence so when we trigger an action  the dispatcher will get notified once  the dispatcher has dealt with an action  the stores listening to it will get  triggered the view gets updated when the  state of the store changes user action  at the view is sent to the dispatcher to  then be processed how is redux different  from flux redux is an open source  javascript library used to manage  application state the store state is  immutable it can only have a single  store and it uses the concept of reducer  flux on the other hand is an  architecture and not a framework or  library the store state is mutable it  can have multiple stores and it uses the  concept of dispatcher let's look at some  react router questions what is a react  router a rear router is a package which  is used to create routing in a react  application react router is used for  developing single page web applications  it allows multiple views in a single  application by defining multiple routes  in that react application how is react  routing different from conventional  routing react routing has a single html  page it uses or the end user rather  would navigate multiple views within the  same file called a single page app the  page does not refresh since it's a  single page file and there is improved  performance since you are not navigating  across multiple pages conventional  routing each view is a separate html  file the user would navigate multiple  files for each view the page would  refresh every time the user navigates  which would hence result in slower  performance how do you implement react  routing you can implement react routing  using a very simple method considering  the above components let's say you've  got a component called app about and  contact so here you can specify the  route path if the route part is just  slash the route defaults out it takes  you to the app component if the route is  slash about in the url given by the end  user you automatically navigate and  activate and load the about component  and if the url is slash contact it would  take you to the contact component let's  talk about react styling questions how  do you style react components either you  use inline styling by using simple css  by simply saying color blue and that's  going to be the output of the h1 element  or i could use a javascript object by  specifying a constant simple style  object and specifying a keypair value of  color background color margin font  family and apply that object as the  style parameter which would result in  this style output how do you style reac